# scripts/ is deliberately NOT excluded. The Dockerfile copies two named files
# from it -- the maintenance entry points the cron service runs -- and nothing
# else, so the image contains only those two whatever else sits in the
# directory. Excluding the directory here and copying out of it there is what
# broke the build: R4 and R6 added those COPY lines against a .dockerignore that
# had excluded scripts/ since before either landed, so the image has never built
# since R4. Re-including single files under an excluded directory would also
# work, but it depends on .dockerignore negation semantics; naming what to copy
# in the Dockerfile does not.
